<title>CHILE: Chile cenbank in talks with HSBC.</title>
<headline>Chile cenbank in talks with HSBC.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's Central Bank is in talks to sell the Hong Kong Shanghai Bank (HSBC) its option to buy shares in Banco Santiago's forthcoming capital increase, said Central Bank president Carlos Massad.</p>
<p>&quot;Yes, we are negotiating the sale of the option,&quot; Massad told reporters.</p>
<p>The Central Bank owns 38.5 percent of Banco Santiago as a result of shares it received in a deal last year to settle a $1.6 billion subordinated debt owed to it by the now-defunct Banco de Santiago.</p>
